@* AdminProducts.razor — Phase 3.3 (refactored to AdminUsers pattern)

   Staff-facing product catalog management page at route `/Admin/Products`.
   Reached from the sidebar's "Admin → Manage Products" link (already wired in
   MainLayout.razor). Role-gated to Admin / Manager / Employee via
   [Authorize(Roles=...)] — customers and read-only users get a 403.

   PURPOSE:
     This page is the staff counterpart to the customer-facing /Products
     catalog. It exists so staff can:
       1. See ALL products in a compact, paginated table (mirrors AdminUsers).
       2. Add a new product → navigates to /Admin/Products/Create.
       3. Restock an existing product (IncreaseProductStockCommand).
       4. Deactivate a product (DeactivateProductCommand — sets StockQuantity
          to 0; see the command's XML doc for why this is the deactivation
          operation). Deactivation is gated by a popup that warns the user
          that the previous stock value will be lost.
       5. View a product's full details → /Products/{Id} (the customer
          detail page already exists; we just link to it).

   STYLE PARITY WITH ADMINUSERS:
     Phase 3.3 refactor — this page now mirrors AdminUsers.razor's structure
     and styling:
       - Same .admin-header layout (icon + page heading + primary action button).
       - Same RadzenDataGrid configuration: AllowSorting, AllowFiltering with
         FilterMode.SimpleWithMenu, AllowPaging with PageSize=20, RowRender
         hook for opacity-cue on rows in a "down" state.
       - Same per-column FilterTemplate pattern for dropdown filters
         (colored badge + AllowClear).
       - Same .row-actions flex container for the Actions column buttons.
       - Same loading / error / empty state markup.

   COLUMNS (in order — Actions is LAST; do NOT wrap any column in
   <AuthorizeView> because that re-orders columns at render time — see the
   comment block on the Sales.razor fix in this same session):
     1. Picture (60px, no filter, no sort)
     2. Name (text filter, clickable link to /Products/{Id})
     3. Price (text filter on Price.Amount, right-aligned tabular-nums)
     4. Stock (text filter, colored: green=in-stock, amber=low ≤10, red=out)
     5. Category (text filter, shows "(deactivated)" suffix if the referenced
        Category has been soft-deleted)
     6. Sub-Category (text filter, "(deactivated)" suffix when applicable;
        em-dash when product has no sub-category)
     7. Sub-Sub-Category (text filter, same pattern as Sub-Category)
     8. Status (dropdown filter: All / In stock / Out of stock — colored
        badges; Out-of-stock = red, In-stock = green)
     9. Actions (View + Restock + Deactivate; last column; no filter)

   DEACTIVATION FLOW (matches the user's spec):
     1. User clicks the Deactivate icon (block icon, Danger color) on a row
        whose StockQuantity > 0.
     2. A Radzen dialog opens (DeactivateProductDialog.razor) explaining:
        "Deactivating this product means its stock becomes 0. If you still
        have some in stock but want it deactivated, write down the current
        stock number yourself — the system does not remember it. Confirm?"
        The dialog shows the current stock value for clarity.
     3. If the user clicks Confirm, DeactivateProductCommand is dispatched
        (sets StockQuantity to 0). On success: toast + grid reload. The
        row's Stock column now shows 0 in red, the Status column shows
        "Out of stock" (red badge), and the row itself is rendered at
        reduced opacity (RowRender hook).
     4. If the user clicks Cancel (or X / Esc), no command is dispatched.

     For products whose StockQuantity is already 0, the Deactivate button
     is HIDDEN (the product is already deactivated — there's nothing to do).
     A Restock button is shown instead so the user can reactivate.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All button clicks are async event handlers
     that dispatch commands via Wolverine. The Blazor circuit's anti-forgery
     token is established at circuit start. *@

@page "/Admin/Products"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager,Employee")]
@attribute [SuppressMessage("Usage", "BL0005:Component parameters should not be set outside their component", Justification = "Radzen exposes FilterValue/FilterOperator on RadzenDataGridColumn as the official programmatic filter API per https://radzen.com/documentation/blazor/data-grid-programmatic-filter/. The BL0005 analyzer (designed for plain Blazor component params) does not understand this Radzen-specific contract; the mutations are intentional and load-bearing.")]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Interfaces
@using TakOne.Application.Products.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Queries.GetProductsPaginated
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.IncreaseProductStock
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Commands.DeactivateProduct
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@using TakOne.WebUI.Components.Dialogs.DeactivateProductDialog
@using TakOne.WebUI.Components.Dialogs.RestockProductDialog
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject ICurrentUserService CurrentUser
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<AdminProducts> Loc
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject Radzen.DialogService DialogService

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            /* Page header — mirrors AdminUsers.razor's .admin-header layout
                                               so the two pages read as members of the same family. */
            .admin-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: space-between;
                gap: 1rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            .product-thumb {
                width: 40px;
                height: 40px;
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
                border-radius: 4px;
                overflow: hidden;
            }

                .product-thumb img {
                    width: 100%;
                    height: 100%;
                    object-fit: contain;
                }

                .product-thumb .rz-icon {
                    font-size: 1.4rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                }

            .stock-cell {
                font-weight: 600;
            }

            .stock-cell-out {
                color: var(--rz-danger);
            }

            .stock-cell-low {
                color: var(--rz-warning);
            }

            .stock-cell-in {
                color: var(--rz-success);
            }

            /* Category-name cell — when the referenced category is deactivated,
                                       we render the name followed by a small red "(deactivated)" badge.
                                       The flex layout keeps the name + badge on one line and lets them
                                       wrap gracefully on narrow viewports. */
            .cat-cell {
                display: inline-flex;
                align-items: center;
                gap: 0.35rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            .cat-deactivated-badge {
                font-size: 0.7rem;
                font-weight: 600;
                color: var(--rz-danger);
                border: 1px solid var(--rz-danger);
                border-radius: 9999px;
                padding: 0.05rem 0.4rem;
                text-transform: uppercase;
                letter-spacing: 0.02em;
                opacity: 0.85;
            }

            .cat-empty {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-style: italic;
            }

            .row-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.25rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                align-items: center;
            }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Page header ── *@
    <div class="admin-header">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
            <RadzenIcon Icon="inventory" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PageHeading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
        </RadzenStack>

        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CreateProductButton"]"
                      Icon="add"
                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                      Variant="Variant.Filled"
                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Products/Create", forceLoad: false))" />
    </div>

    @* ── Loading spinner ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center"
                     Style="height: 40vh;" Gap="1rem">
            <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false"
                                       Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate"
                                       Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Large" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["LoadingText"]"
                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
        </RadzenStack>
    }

    @* ── Error banner ── *@
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_loadError))
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadProductsAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── Empty state ── *@
    else if (_products.Count == 0)
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 3rem; text-align: center;">
            <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="1rem">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="inventory_2" Style="font-size: 3rem; color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["EmptyTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["EmptyMessage"]"
                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); max-width: 420px;" />
                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CreateFirstProductButton"]"
                              Icon="add"
                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                              Variant="Variant.Filled"
                              Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Products/Create", forceLoad: false))" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Product table ──
       Mirrors AdminUsers.razor's RadzenDataGrid configuration. All filtering
       is client-side via the per-column FilterTemplate (no external filter
       bar). Loads all products in one round-trip (PageSize=100 = backend cap)
       and lets Radzen handle client-side filter + paging. The grid uses
       AllowColumnReorder="false" so the source-order columns are respected
       (defense against stale persisted reorder state from a prior session).
       IMPORTANT: do NOT wrap any <RadzenDataGridColumn> in <AuthorizeView> —
       that re-orders columns at render time. See Sales.razor's comment for
       the full root-cause explanation. *@
    else
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Class="admin-products-grid" Style="padding: 0.5rem;">
            <RadzenDataGrid @ref="grid"
                            Data="@_products"
                            TItem="ProductListItemDto"
                            AllowSorting="true"
                            AllowFiltering="true"
                            FilterMode="FilterMode.SimpleWithMenu"
                            FilterCaseSensitivity="FilterCaseSensitivity.CaseInsensitive"
                            AllowPaging="true"
                            PageSize="20"
                            PagerHorizontalAlign="HorizontalAlign.Center"
                            EmptyText="@Loc["EmptyText"]"
                            AllowColumnReorder="false"
                            Style="width: 100%;"
                            RowRender="@OnRowRender">
                <Columns>

                    @* ── Picture — no filter, no sort, fixed width ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="ProductListItemDto"
                                          Width="60px"
                                          Sortable="false"
                                          Filterable="false">
                        <Template Context="product">
                            <div class="product-thumb">
                                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(product.PictureUrl))
                                {
                                    <img src="@product.PictureUrl" alt="@product.Name" loading="lazy" />
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <RadzenIcon Icon="image" />
                                }
                            </div>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Name — text filter, clickable link to /Products/{Id} ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="ProductListItemDto"
                                          Property="Name"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColName"]"
                                          Width="*">
                        <Template Context="product">
                            <RadzenLink Text="@product.Name"
                                        Path="@($"/Products/{product.Id}")"
                                        Style="font-weight: 600;" />
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Price — text filter on Price.Amount, right-aligned ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="ProductListItemDto"
                                          Property="Price.Amount"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColPrice"]"
                                          Width="140px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Right">
                        <Template Context="product">
                            <span style="font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;">@FormatPrice(product.Price)</span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Stock — text filter, color-coded (red=0, amber ≤10, green >10) ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="ProductListItemDto"
                                          Property="StockQuantity"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColStock"]"
                                          Width="100px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Right">
                        <Template Context="product">
                            <span class="stock-cell @GetStockClass(product.StockQuantity)">
                                @string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, "{0:N0}", product.StockQuantity)
                            </span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Category — text filter, "(deactivated)" badge when CategoryIsActive=false ──
                       The Property is bound to CategoryName so Radzen's text
                       filter operates on the resolved display name (not the
                       Guid). The deactivated badge is appended in the
                       Template; it's not part of the filter value. *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="ProductListItemDto"
                                          Property="CategoryName"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColCategory"]"
                                          Width="200px">
                        <Template Context="product">
                            <span class="cat-cell">
                                @if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(product.CategoryName))
                                {
                                    <span class="cat-empty">@Loc["UnknownCategory"]</span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <span>@product.CategoryName</span>
                                }
                                @if (!product.CategoryIsActive)
                                {
                                    <span class="cat-deactivated-badge">@Loc["DeactivatedSuffix"]</span>
                                }
                            </span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Sub-Category — text filter, em-dash when null, "(deactivated)" when inactive ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="ProductListItemDto"
                                          Property="SubCategoryName"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColSubCategory"]"
                                          Width="200px">
                        <Template Context="product">
                            <span class="cat-cell">
                                @if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(product.SubCategoryName))
                                {
                                    <span class="cat-empty">@Loc["NoSubCategory"]</span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <span>@product.SubCategoryName</span>
                                }
                                @if (!product.SubCategoryIsActive)
                                {
                                    <span class="cat-deactivated-badge">@Loc["DeactivatedSuffix"]</span>
                                }
                            </span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Sub-Sub-Category — text filter, em-dash when null, "(deactivated)" when inactive ── *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="ProductListItemDto"
                                          Property="SubSubCategoryName"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColSubSubCategory"]"
                                          Width="200px">
                        <Template Context="product">
                            <span class="cat-cell">
                                @if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(product.SubSubCategoryName))
                                {
                                    <span class="cat-empty">@Loc["NoSubSubCategory"]</span>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    <span>@product.SubSubCategoryName</span>
                                }
                                @if (!product.SubSubCategoryIsActive)
                                {
                                    <span class="cat-deactivated-badge">@Loc["DeactivatedSuffix"]</span>
                                }
                            </span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Status — dropdown filter with colored badges ──
                       Two-state filter mirroring AdminUsers' Status column:
                       "In stock" (StockQuantity > 0, green badge) vs
                       "Out of stock" (StockQuantity == 0, red badge).
                       The dropdown uses string keys mapped to a custom
                       filter that compares StockQuantity > 0 (In stock) or
                       == 0 (Out of stock). AllowClear resets to null (All). *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="ProductListItemDto"
                                          Property="StockQuantity"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColStatus"]"
                                          Width="140px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Center"
                                          FilterOperator="FilterOperator.Equals">
                        <Template Context="product">
                            <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(product.StockQuantity > 0)"
                                         BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(product.StockQuantity > 0)"
                                         IsPill="true" />
                        </Template>
                        <FilterTemplate Context="column">
                            <RadzenDropDown @bind-Value="_selectedStatusFilter"
                                            Data="@_statusFilterOptions"
                                            TValue="string"
                                            AllowClear="true"
                                            Placeholder="@Loc["StatusAll"]"
                                            Change="@(args => OnStatusFilterChanged(_selectedStatusFilter, column))"
                                            Style="width: 100%; min-width: 130px;">
                                <ValueTemplate Context="selected">
                                    @{
                                        var selectedStr = selected?.ToString();
                                    }
                                    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(selectedStr))
                                    {
                                        <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(selectedStr)"
                                                     BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(selectedStr)"
                                                     IsPill="true" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <span>@Loc["StatusAll"]</span>
                                    }
                                </ValueTemplate>
                                <Template Context="statusOption">
                                    @{
                                        var optStr = statusOption?.ToString();
                                    }
                                    <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(optStr)"
                                                 BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(optStr)"
                                                 IsPill="true" />
                                </Template>
                            </RadzenDropDown>
                        </FilterTemplate>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* ── Actions — View + Restock + Deactivate (last column; no filter) ──
                       Three icon-only text buttons:
                       - visibility (Info) → navigates to /Products/{Id}
                       - add_circle_outline (Success) → opens Restock prompt
                         (always available — restocking an already-in-stock
                         product just adds more)
                       - block (Danger) → opens DeactivateProductDialog ONLY
                         when StockQuantity > 0. When StockQuantity is already
                         0, the Deactivate button is HIDDEN (the product is
                         already deactivated; Restock is the only action). *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="ProductListItemDto"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColActions"]"
                                          Width="160px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Center"
                                          Sortable="false"
                                          Filterable="false">
                        <Template Context="product">
                            <div class="row-actions">
                                <RadzenButton Icon="visibility"
                                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Info"
                                              title="@Loc["ActionView"]"
                                              aria-label="@Loc["ActionView"]"
                                              Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo($"/Products/{product.Id}", forceLoad: false))" />

                                <RadzenButton Icon="add_circle_outline"
                                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Success"
                                              title="@Loc["ActionRestock"]"
                                              aria-label="@Loc["ActionRestock"]"
                                              Disabled="@(_isBusyProductId == product.Id)"
                                              Click="@(() => HandleRestockAsync(product))" />

                                @if (product.StockQuantity > 0)
                                {
                                    <RadzenButton Icon="block"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                  title="@Loc["ActionDeactivate"]"
                                                  aria-label="@Loc["ActionDeactivate"]"
                                                  Disabled="@(_isBusyProductId == product.Id)"
                                                  Click="@(() => HandleDeactivateAsync(product))" />
                                }
                            </div>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>
                </Columns>
            </RadzenDataGrid>
        </RadzenCard>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── State ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private List<ProductListItemDto> _products = new();
    private RadzenDataGrid<ProductListItemDto> grid = default!;

    // Status filter state — null = "no filter" (AllowClear=true on the
    // RadzenDropDown passes null when the user clears).
    private string? _selectedStatusFilter;

    // Status filter options — string keys "InStock"/"OutOfStock"
    // (culture-neutral). The display text comes from GetStatusLabel(string).
    private readonly List<string> _statusFilterOptions = new()
    {
        "InStock", "OutOfStock"
    };

    private bool _isLoading = true;
    private string _loadError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The Id of the product whose action button is currently in flight.
    /// Null when no action is pending. Used to disable that row's action
    /// buttons while the round-trip is in progress (prevents double-clicks).
    /// </summary>
    private Guid? _isBusyProductId;

    // ── Lifecycle ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            await LoadProductsAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadProductsAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;
        _loadError = string.Empty;

        try
        {
            // Load up to 100 products (the backend cap) so the grid has
            // enough rows for client-side filtering + paging. Same approach
            // as AdminUsers.razor.
            //
            // IncludeInactive=true so deactivated (zero-stock) products are
            // visible to staff. The handler enforces role-gating on this
            // flag — non-staff callers silently get active-only.
            var query = new GetProductsPaginatedQuery
            {
                PageNumber = 1,
                PageSize = 100,
                SearchTerm = null,
                CategoryId = null,
                IncludeInactive = true
            };

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<PaginatedResult<ProductListItemDto>>(query);
            _products = result.Items.ToList();
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _loadError = Loc["Error_FailedToLoad"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Filter handlers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Status filter handler. Maps the string key ("InStock"/"OutOfStock")
    /// to a Radzen filter on the StockQuantity column:
    ///   - "InStock"     → FilterOperator.GreaterThan, FilterValue = 0
    ///   - "OutOfStock"  → FilterOperator.Equals,      FilterValue = 0
    ///   - null / empty  → clear the filter (All)
    /// </summary>
    private async Task OnStatusFilterChanged(string? value, RadzenDataGridColumn<ProductListItemDto> column)
    {
        _selectedStatusFilter = value;

        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(value))
        {
            column.FilterValue = null;
        }
        else if (value == "InStock")
        {
            column.FilterValue = 0;
            column.FilterOperator = FilterOperator.GreaterThan;
        }
        else // "OutOfStock"
        {
            column.FilterValue = 0;
            column.FilterOperator = FilterOperator.Equals;
        }

        await grid.Reload();
    }

    // ── Restock ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Opens the RestockProductDialog (a Radzen dialog component) so the
    /// user can enter the quantity to add to the product's stock. On
    /// Confirm, dispatches <see cref="IncreaseProductStockCommand"/>.
    ///
    /// WHY A DIALOG (not JS prompt()):
    ///   The user explicitly asked for a "proper popup" — the previous
    ///   implementation used the browser's native prompt(), which is
    ///   ugly, unstyled, un-themeable, and doesn't render localized
    ///   text correctly in some browsers. The custom dialog gives us:
    ///     1. The product name (so the user knows which product
    ///        they're restocking without scrolling back to the grid).
    ///     2. The current stock value (so the user can see how much
    ///        is already there before deciding how much to add).
    ///     3. A RadzenNumeric input with Min=1, Step=1, spinner
    ///        arrows — much nicer UX than a free-text JS prompt.
    ///     4. Inline validation in the dialog itself (no need to
    ///        Toast.Warning on bad input — the dialog handles it).
    ///   The dialog returns a positive int if the user confirmed, or
    ///   null/false otherwise.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleRestockAsync(ProductListItemDto product)
    {
        if (_isBusyProductId.HasValue) return;

        object? result;
        try
        {
            result = await DialogService.OpenAsync<RestockProductDialog>(
                Loc["RestockDialogTitle"],
                new Dictionary<string, object?>
                {
                    { "ProductName", product.Name },
                    { "CurrentStock", product.StockQuantity }
                },
                new Radzen.DialogOptions
                {
                    Width = "460px",
                    Resizable = false,
                    Draggable = true,
                    CloseDialogOnOverlayClick = false,  // force the user to click a button — no accidental close
                    ShowClose = true                    // keep the X button so the user has an obvious escape
                });
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            System.Console.WriteLine($"Restock dialog open failed: {ex.Message}");
            await Toast.Error(Loc["RestockDialogError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        // DialogService.Close(object) boxes the int. Anything that isn't
        // a positive int is treated as "user aborted" (covers null,
        // false, dismissed-via-X/Esc cases). The dialog itself already
        // validates that the entered value is a positive int before
        // calling Close(value), so we don't need to re-validate here.
        if (result is not int quantity || quantity <= 0) return;

        _isBusyProductId = product.Id;
        try
        {
            var command = new IncreaseProductStockCommand(product.Id, quantity);
            var cmdResult = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(command);

            if (cmdResult.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["RestockSuccess"], quantity, product.Name),
                    summary: Loc["RestockSuccessTitle"]);
                await LoadProductsAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(cmdResult.Error ?? Loc["RestockError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["RestockError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusyProductId = null;
        }
    }

    // ── Deactivate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Opens the DeactivateProductDialog (a Radzen dialog component) that
    /// warns the user about the stock-loss implication and asks for
    /// confirmation. On Confirm, dispatches DeactivateProductCommand.
    ///
    /// WHY A DIALOG (not JS confirm()):
    ///   The user's spec explicitly asks for a popup that EXPLAINS the
    ///   implication ("deactivating means stock becomes 0; if you still
    ///   have inventory, write down the current stock number yourself")
    ///   and shows the current stock value for clarity. JS confirm() is
    ///   too sparse for that — we need a custom dialog with formatted
    ///   text + the current stock value. The dialog returns true if the
    ///   user confirmed, false/null if they cancelled.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleDeactivateAsync(ProductListItemDto product)
    {
        if (_isBusyProductId.HasValue) return;

        // Guard: only show the dialog if there's stock to lose. The
        // markup also hides the button when StockQuantity == 0, but
        // defense-in-depth never hurts.
        if (product.StockQuantity <= 0)
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["AlreadyDeactivated"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        object? confirmed;
        try
        {
            confirmed = await DialogService.OpenAsync<DeactivateProductDialog>(
                Loc["DeactivateDialogTitle"],
                new Dictionary<string, object?>
                {
                    { "ProductName", product.Name },
                    { "CurrentStock", product.StockQuantity }
                },
                new Radzen.DialogOptions
                {
                    Width = "460px",
                    Resizable = false,
                    Draggable = true,
                    CloseDialogOnOverlayClick = false,  // force the user to click a button — no accidental close
                    ShowClose = true                    // keep the X button so the user has an obvious escape
                });
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            System.Console.WriteLine($"Deactivate dialog open failed: {ex.Message}");
            await Toast.Error(Loc["DeactivateDialogError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        // DialogService.Close(object) boxes a bool. Anything that isn't
        // exactly `true` is treated as "user aborted" (covers false, null,
        // and dismissed-via-X/Esc cases).
        if (confirmed is not true) return;

        _isBusyProductId = product.Id;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new DeactivateProductCommand(product.Id));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["DeactivateSuccess"], product.Name),
                    summary: Loc["DeactivateSuccessTitle"]);
                await LoadProductsAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(result.Error ?? Loc["DeactivateError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["DeactivateError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusyProductId = null;
        }
    }

    // ── Row render hook ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void OnRowRender(RowRenderEventArgs<ProductListItemDto> args)
    {
        // Subtle visual cue for out-of-stock rows: slight opacity.
        // Mirrors AdminUsers.razor's OnRowRender for inactive users.
        // Per-row coloring beyond this is handled by the stock-cell CSS
        // class on the stock column itself.
        if (args.Data is { } p && p.StockQuantity == 0)
        {
            args.Attributes.Add("style", "opacity: 0.65;");
        }
    }

    // ── Display helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a MoneyDto for display. IRR is labelled "ریال" (no division —
    /// admin pages show the real Rial amount stored in the database).
    /// Other currencies pass through unchanged.
    /// </summary>
    private static string FormatPrice(MoneyDto? price)
    {
        if (price is null) return "—";
        var isIrr = string.Equals(price.Currency, "IRR", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);
        var unit = isIrr ? "ریال" : price.Currency;
        return $"{price.Amount.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)} {unit}";
    }

    private static string GetStockClass(int stock)
    {
        if (stock == 0) return "stock-cell-out";
        if (stock <= 10) return "stock-cell-low";
        return "stock-cell-in";
    }

    // ── Status helpers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Used by both the cell Template (bool overload — stock > 0) and the
    // filter dropdown's ValueTemplate/Template (string overload —
    // "InStock"/"OutOfStock" keys).

    private string GetStatusLabel(bool inStock)
        => inStock ? Loc["StatusInStockBadge"] : Loc["StatusOutOfStockBadge"];

    private string GetStatusLabel(string? status)
        => status switch
        {
            "InStock" => Loc["StatusInStock"],
            "OutOfStock" => Loc["StatusOutOfStock"],
            _ => Loc["StatusAll"]
        };

    private BadgeStyle GetStatusBadgeStyle(bool inStock)
        => inStock ? BadgeStyle.Success : BadgeStyle.Danger;

    private BadgeStyle GetStatusBadgeStyle(string? status)
        => status switch
        {
            "InStock" => BadgeStyle.Success,
            "OutOfStock" => BadgeStyle.Danger,
            _ => BadgeStyle.Base
        };
}